    title: "‘Russia wants more than Ukraine,’ says Germany’s Merz as he defends aid for Kyiv",
    summary: "German Chancellor Friedrich Merz said that by supporting Ukraine, Germany was also protecting itself.",
    preview: "Berlin – German Chancellor Friedrich Merz accused Russia on Wednesday of “escalating” threats to European security as he defended his government’s plans to bolster defense spending and maintain financial aid to Ukraine. Opposition parties, including the far-right Alternative for Germany (AfD), which tops national opinion polls, and the hard-left Die Linke, have called for an end to military aid to Kyiv. “It cannot be said often enough, against the far right as much as the far left: Russia knows exactly what it wants.",
    body: "Berlin – German Chancellor Friedrich Merz accused Russia on Wednesday of “escalating” threats to European security as he defended his government’s plans to bolster defense spending and maintain financial aid to Ukraine.\n\nOpposition parties, including the far-right Alternative for Germany (AfD), which tops national opinion polls, and the hard-left Die Linke, have called for an end to military aid to Kyiv.\n\n“It cannot be said often enough, against the far right as much as the far left: Russia knows exactly what it wants. And Russia wants more than Ukraine,” Merz told the Bundestag lower house of parliament during a debate on the 2027 draft budget.",
