    body: "Saudi-led coalition says it intercepts Houthi drone near Jeddah Islamic Port The Saudi-led coalition said on Wednesday it intercepted and destroyed a drone launched by Yemen's Iran-aligned Houthis near Jeddah Islamic Port on Saudi Arabia's Red Sea coast, adding that no civilians were injured by debris from the interception. The Houthis said they had attacked the port. Jeddah Islamic Port is a major Saudi maritime gateway on the Red Sea and a key hub for cargo and container traffic.\n\nA picture taken on 1 March 2022 shows a view of cranes and shipping containers at a loading dock of Jeddah's Islamic Seaport on Saudi Arabia's western Red Sea coast (AFP)",
