    title: "UK moving military planes into hangars amid drone threat: Reports",
    summary: "UK moving military planes into hangars amid drone threat: Reports Britain's air force is moving planes into hangars and hardened shelters overnight to protect them from drone threats, The Times and Sky News reported on Wednesday. The two UK media outlets also revealed plans by the Royal Air Force (RAF) to install anti-drone nets around warplanes that remain exposed. The Ministry of Defence did not confirm the reports, but in a statement to AFP said it takes \"the security of our bases, equipment and personnel very seriously and (is) always adapting to counter any potential threats\". The ministry said it was \"investing an additional £470 million ($615 million) to strengthen security at military sites, including better physical protection, surveillance and counter-drone capabilities\". British authorities have regularly issued warnings about the threats posed by Russia and Iran and the government has urged the country to be prepared for different contingencies.",
    preview: "UK moving military planes into hangars amid drone threat: Reports Britain's air force is moving planes into hangars and hardened shelters overnight to protect them from drone threats, The Times and Sky News reported on Wednesday. The two UK media outlets also revealed plans by the Royal Air Force (RAF) to install anti-drone nets around warplanes that remain exposed.",
    body: "UK moving military planes into hangars amid drone threat: Reports Britain's air force is moving planes into hangars and hardened shelters overnight to protect them from drone threats, The Times and Sky News reported on Wednesday. The two UK media outlets also revealed plans by the Royal Air Force (RAF) to install anti-drone nets around warplanes that remain exposed. The Ministry of Defence did not confirm the reports, but in a statement to AFP said it takes \"the security of our bases, equipment and personnel very seriously and (is) always adapting to counter any potential threats\".\n\nThe ministry said it was \"investing an additional £470 million ($615 million) to strengthen security at military sites, including better physical protection, surveillance and counter-drone capabilities\". British authorities have regularly issued warnings about the threats posed by Russia and Iran and the government has urged the country to be prepared for different contingencies.",
