    title: "For Trump, doubling down on tariffs is about power, not popularity",
    summary: "The administration new tariffs on 14 major trading partners, a seemingly counterintuitive move that reflects Trump's belief in tariffs and a new political reality.",
    preview: "PALM BEACH, Florida – In midterm elections three weeks ago, U.S. voters punished Republicans over an economy and inflation that many said were made worse by tariffs. President Donald Trump is doubling down on them anyway. The Trump administration on Wednesday announced a new round of tariffs on goods from 14 major trading partners, including China, Japan and the European Union, a seemingly counterintuitive move that reflects both Trump’s decades-old belief in tariffs and a new political reality confronting his White House.",
    body: "PALM BEACH, Florida – In midterm elections three weeks ago, U.S. voters punished Republicans over an economy and inflation that many said were made worse by tariffs. President Donald Trump is doubling down on them anyway.\n\nThe Trump administration on Wednesday announced a new round of tariffs on goods from 14 major trading partners, including China, Japan and the European Union, a seemingly counterintuitive move that reflects both Trump’s decades-old belief in tariffs and a new political reality confronting his White House.\n\nWith Democrats set to control Congress for the final two years of his presidency, tariffs are taking on added importance as one of the most potent economic tools Trump can wield without lawmakers’ approval.",
